Z||000002||West Coast Fiero||12-16-2001||02:21 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Sootah:<BR><B>Allright, now I don't expect anything from this (well, other than some of the more hot-headed members of this forum makeing fun of me) but I need  either a co-signer or a loan. My 85 GT (see sig) tossed a rod and I can no longer use the car I have been borrowing up until now. This wouldn't be a big deal as I could ride a bike or something if it were not for the fact that I live 14 miles out of town. Now you see the rather desperate situation I am in.<P>I'm 19, working 2 jobs, and have no real expenses (Living w/ parents. Yes, it is sad). They would sign with me but they are rather strapped at the moment as they just got this house. My father is an ass; after coming to live with my mother he has essentially disowned me so he won't help. I have also asked my uncle but he is on my fathers side of the family and my dad has a rather large mouth. Banks will not touch me because I have no previous credit history (19).<P>For a co-signer I'd give $100, or for a loan straight from you I'd use the title to the car as collateral and be willing to pay some higher interest. The title would actually be decent collateral seeing as soon as I have the funds there will be an engine going into the car.<P>E-Mail me for contact info if you want to speak directly to me. PM if you'd like but I don't check that all that often (don't ever remember to).<P>*Dons abspestos suit*<P>Thank you,<BR>    [b]<I>-Sootah</B></I><P>[/B]<HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Too bad this didnt happen 5 months ago, at that time we had literally thrown away 2 complete 2.8's, one with 80,000 miles, and the other with 60,000 from cars that were recipients of 3.4's. If I still had these I would take the best of both and make one strong motor for you, ship it up to you, and say Merry Christmas.<P>  We currently do not have any engine conversions lined up, however if we do come across a decent short block we will not hesitate to ship it to you - we will keep you posted.....<P> <BR> <P>------------------<BR>Technician, West Coast Fiero<BR>www.cwestco.com<BR>310-305-4111||||reg||1
Z||000003||fierospeeder||12-16-2001||03:19 AM||||do you have a girlfriend, or a close friend/cousin that can cosign.<P><BR>I had to get a loan for my g/f and i would get it but i needed a cosigner, and she had to sign it.  I have no real credit history except 2 cc i had for a year.   I didn't need the loan cause my g/f moved but i can always get the loan if i needed it.<P><BR>Talk to the loaner, and see if you can get a loan for 2000.  Tell him your situation, you got two jobs, pay check stubs, your friend is willing to help you out.   etc..<P>I would check a local bank out, or a bank which your mom got the loan for the house.  ||||reg||1
Z||000004||SCCA FIERO||12-16-2001||03:34 AM||||I have a 2.8 sitting around that MIGHT run. It was given to me and I have no clue if it runs, but I was told it does. I need to get a few parts from it and maybe you can have the rest. I have no idea when I will get around to doing this. I'll try to get over there tomorrow and pull the stuff I want(timing cover, oil pan, and other minor things) and you can have the block. I could deliver it in my truck if needed.<P>Merry Xmas.||||reg||1
