Z||000009||My7Fieros||12-16-2001||04:33 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by West Coast Fiero:<BR><B> Too bad this didnt happen 5 months ago, at that time we had literally thrown away 2 complete 2.8's, one with 80,000 miles, and the other with 60,000 from cars that were recipients of 3.4's.<P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><BR>O..k...and my question would be....why?  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smiley_wtf.gif"><P>||||reg||1
Z||000010||West Coast Fiero||12-16-2001||09:05 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by My7Fieros:<BR><B> [QUOTE]Originally posted by West Coast Fiero:<BR>[b] Too bad this didnt happen 5 months ago, at that time we had literally thrown away 2 complete 2.8's, one with 80,000 miles, and the other with 60,000 from cars that were recipients of 3.4's.<P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><BR>O..k...and my question would be....why?   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smiley_wtf.gif"><P>[/B][/QUOTE]<P><BR>If we were to keep every engine from every car we do a conversion to, we would have a large portion of the shop that would be storage for used engines, similar to Mr. Archibald's shop. We do not have the room, time, and over head to store used engines with a minimal lifespan. However if there is a need for these engines is there a person here I can contact to make aware that we have an engine or engines that could use a home. I have an updated list of all drivetrain parts we currently have at all times, perhaps this would benifit someone.<P> So to some it up, we just throw the 2.8's straight into the big blue dumpster in trade for a 3800, 3.4 TDC, 3.4 PR, 4.1,4.5,4.6 NS, 4.9 and soon to be 302,305,327, and 350 series engines<BR><P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://clubs.hemmings.com/fieroswest/WestCoast300.gif"> <BR>Eric Nelson<BR>Technician,<BR>West Coast Fiero<BR>www.cwestco.com<BR>310-305-4111||||reg||1
Z||000011||My7Fieros||12-16-2001||10:22 PM||||Ok, not trying to be an ass or anything, so dont get me wrong. But 80,000 and 60,000 Fiero 2.8's are actually pretty low milage engines. These things dont exactly grow on trees. Call Ed Parks @ the Fiero Factory. Im sure he'd be interested. I see Ed roughly once a week (I usually drive down there on Thursdays). Matter of fact I just bought an 80k mile 2.8 from him to put in an 87 GT I have w/no engine. You may be able to make some $$ from those engines you throw away.||||reg||1
Z||000012||West Coast Fiero||12-16-2001||10:43 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by My7Fieros:<BR><B>Ok, not trying to be an ass or anything, so dont get me wrong. But 80,000 and 60,000 Fiero 2.8's are actually pretty low milage engines. These things dont exactly grow on trees. Call Ed Parks @ the Fiero Factory. Im sure he'd be interested. I see Ed roughly once a week (I usually drive down there on Thursdays). Matter of fact I just bought an 80k mile 2.8 from him to put in an 87 GT I have w/no engine. You may be able to make some $$ from those engines you throw away.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>This may be a viable solution, as our customers want nothing to do with the engines we remove which had left us with no other choice.<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://clubs.hemmings.com/fieroswest/WestCoast300.gif"> <BR>Eric Nelson<BR>Technician,<BR>West Coast Fiero<BR>www.cwestco.com<BR>310-305-4111||||reg||1
Z||000013||Sootah||12-17-2001||12:55 AM||||You guys kick ass. I'd still need $ to put the engine in, since I have the whole 2 jobs thing and don't have the time to do it myself. Although I could scrounge up the $ to get her slapped in reasonable quickly. Keep me posted guys.<P><B>PEACE  <I>-Sootah</B></I>||||reg||7
