Z||000032||West Coast Fiero||12-30-2001||06:36 PM||||The oppurtunity to do this is still Here. I spoke with Chris and he said that I will be doing this on my time, as there is much overhead here at the shop. The only time I can honestly see myself getting anytime on the car would be the end of Jan as I am still finishing up on Keith Huff's Northstar, and I always have no less than 4 fix-it jobs going on at the same time...<P>so where we stand:<BR><LI> the engine is over on a palate wrapped in 2 plastic "sleeping bags"<BR><LI> brandnew 88 flywheel is on top of it<BR><LI> a set of injectors that I have reversed cleaned and matched are in a box and ready<BR><LI> I think a WCF Cold Air Intake will mysteriously find its way onto your car<P><BR> do you want to come out with any parts you want to put on at this time, now that the car will be essentially torn apart?<P> is there any body else willing to sponsor the resurection of this car...<P><B>Rodney Dickman</B> - I'd love to see a set of steel vacum lines on here<BR> <BR><B>Fiero Shop</B> - any parts you would care to donate?<P> I will keep everyone posted, hopefully as time progresses we will soon find a stockpile of parts that will help out Sootah<P><P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://clubs.hemmings.com/fieroswest/WestCoast300.gif"> <BR>Eric Nelson<BR>Technician,<BR>West Coast Fiero<BR>www.cwestco.com<BR>310-305-4111||||reg||1
